---
description: Resolve the requested publication review from actual current scope, retained revision and preflight evidence.
args:
  goal: string
returns: PublicationGoalReport
---
Determine which observed provider, destination, environment and audience the user means, and which retained-review, current-package or existing-operation evidence the question requires. Compose the available discovery, scope interpretation, exact Native binding and semantic evidence branches accordingly. An inspection question is not authorization to upload, submit or change a destination.

Use actual current observation and binding results. If the scope changed or the Native binding is unavailable, decide whether fresh evidence can resolve the request; do not mechanically replay a stale choice or substitute a neighboring target. Independent revision and preflight investigations may be composed together when useful, while an explicit user ordering or an actual data dependency must be preserved.

Return the actual selected scope and the supported requested review values. Keep a missing or blocked boundary explicit rather than inventing completed checks, current approval, a hosted deployment or an unchanged prior review. Protected workspace state and existing operation journals remain untouched by this review.
